{
  "_comment": [
    "Pages the accessibility and contrast gate (scripts/ui_a11y_scan.js, the",
    "`browser-a11y` job in .github/workflows/test.yml) checks in light and dark mode.",
    "Broader than ui_smoke_ci.json on purpose: contrast and naming regressions",
    "land on settings panes, the check-in desk and help as often as on the",
    "match board. Each target is six page loads (two schemes, four phones);",
    "the scan runs six at a time.",
    "",
    "`a11y.ignore` is for a finding that is wrong, not one that is hard. Each",
    "entry names the rule (an axe rule id, or \"contrast\"), optionally the",
    "target, and says why. See docs/style-guide.md#checking-your-change."
  ],
  "loginAs": "staff_user",
  "tenant": "default",
  "outDir": "/tmp/ui-smoke-ci",
  "a11y": {
    "schemes": ["light", "dark"],
    "ignore": []
  },
  "phone": {
    "_comment": "Layout at phone width, on the narrowest and widest phones of the last three years plus the commonest sizes between (360, 393, 412, 440px; a 2026-10 run across nine phones from 360 to 440 found nothing these four miss). Rendered by Chromium with each phone's size, pixel ratio and user agent: nothing scrolls sideways, runs out of its card or is cut off. Layout does not change with the colour scheme, so one pass is enough. `ignore` takes a CSS selector and a why.",
    "devices": [
      "Galaxy S24",
      "iPhone 15 Pro",
      "Pixel 7",
      { "name": "iPhone 16 Pro Max", "viewport": { "width": 440, "height": 956 }, "deviceScaleFactor": 3, "isMobile": true, "hasTouch": true }
    ],
    "schemes": ["light"],
    "ignore": []
  },
  "targets": [
